@node Introduction
@chapter Introduction

@command{waggle} is a from-the-ground-up rederivation of a Hive client that
takes only Node built-ins as given: @code{node:crypto} for SHA-256,
RIPEMD-160, and HMAC, and @code{node:https} for transport. base58, the
secp256k1 curve, and the graphene serializer are hand-rolled. It is named for
the bees' waggle dance, by which a hive shares where to go.

Reads ask a public Hive node for data and need no keys. Writes build, sign,
and broadcast a transaction and need the relevant private key, supplied
through the environment (@pxref{Environment}); waggle never writes keys to
disk.

@node Invocation
@chapter Invocation

@example
waggle @var{command} [@var{arguments}@dots{}]
waggle help | --help | -h
@end example

The first argument is a command. With no command, or with @code{help},
@option{-h}, or @option{--help}, waggle prints a usage summary. Results are
printed to standard output as pretty-printed JSON, or as a bare string for
scalar results. Errors go to standard error prefixed with @samp{waggle:}, and
the exit status is @code{0} on success and non-zero on failure.

@node Read commands
@chapter Read commands

These query a Hive node and require no keys.

@table @code
@item globals
Print the dynamic global properties of the chain.
@item refblock
Print the TaPoS reference data: @code{ref_block_num}, @code{ref_block_prefix},
and the chain head time.
@item account @var{name}
Print the account object for @var{name}.
@item content @var{author} @var{permlink}
Print a post or comment via @code{condenser_api.get_content}.
@item post @var{author} @var{permlink}
Print a post via @code{bridge.get_post}.
@item ranked @var{sort} [@var{tag}] [@var{limit}]
Print ranked posts; @var{sort} is @code{trending}, @code{hot},
@code{created}, and so on.
@item posts @var{account} [@var{sort}] [@var{limit}]
Print an account's posts; @var{sort} is @code{blog}, @code{feed},
@code{posts}, or @code{replies}.
@item profile @var{account}
Print an account's social profile.
@item followers @var{account} [@var{limit}]
Print the accounts following @var{account}.
@item following @var{account} [@var{limit}]
Print the accounts @var{account} follows.
@item follow-count @var{account}
Print follower and following counts.
@item history @var{account} [@var{limit}]
Print the account's operation history.
@end table

@node Write commands
@chapter Write commands

These build, sign, and broadcast a transaction. Social actions use the posting
key (@env{WAGGLE_POSTING_KEY}); value transfers use the active key
(@env{WAGGLE_ACTIVE_KEY}).

@table @code
@item vote @var{author} @var{permlink} [@var{weight}]
Vote on a post. @var{weight} is in basis points and defaults to @code{10000}
(100%). Posting key.
@item unvote @var{author} @var{permlink}
Remove a vote (weight 0). Posting key.
@item publish @var{title} @var{body} [@var{tag}]
Publish a new top-level post. A @var{body} of @samp{-} is read from standard
input. Posting key.
@item reply @var{parentAuthor} @var{parentPermlink} @var{body}
Reply to a post or comment. A @var{body} of @samp{-} is read from standard
input. Posting key.
@item transfer @var{to} @var{amount} [@var{memo}]
Transfer value, e.g.@: @code{"1.000 HIVE"}. The memo is plaintext. Active key.
@item follow @var{account}
Follow @var{account}. Posting key.
@item unfollow @var{account}
Unfollow @var{account}. Posting key.
@item reblog @var{author} @var{permlink}
Reblog a post to your blog. Posting key.
@item claim
Claim all pending rewards for the configured account. Posting key.
@end table

@node Utility commands
@chapter Utility commands

@table @code
@item pubkey @var{wif}
Derive and print the @code{STM} public key for a WIF private key, offline.
@item whoami
Print the configured account and the public keys derived from the configured
private keys.
@item help
Print the usage summary.
@end table

@node Environment
@chapter Environment

@table @env
@item WAGGLE_ACCOUNT
Default account for write commands, and observer for reads that accept one.
@item WAGGLE_POSTING_KEY
WIF posting key, used by @code{vote}, @code{publish}, @code{reply},
@code{follow}, @code{reblog}, and @code{claim}.
@item WAGGLE_ACTIVE_KEY
WIF active key, used by @code{transfer}.
@item WAGGLE_OWNER_KEY
WIF owner key.
@item WAGGLE_MEMO_KEY
WIF memo key.
@item WAGGLE_NODES
Comma-separated node base URLs to use instead of the built-in defaults.
@end table

@node Library
@chapter Library

Everything the command does is available from JavaScript through the
@code{Waggle} class. Reads need no keys; writes take the relevant key per role.

@example
import @{ Waggle @} from "@@561-group/waggle";

const hive = new Waggle();                 // reads, no keys
const [acct] = await hive.getAccounts(["hiveio"]);

const me = new Waggle(@{                    // writes, posting key
  account: "alice",
  keys: @{ posting: process.env.WAGGLE_POSTING_KEY @},
@});
await me.vote(@{ author: "bob", permlink: "a-post", weight: 10000 @});
@end example

The full type surface, with per-method documentation, lives in
@file{lib/client.d.ts}, and the prose mirror in
@file{docs/reference/library-api.md}.

@node Security
@chapter Security

Private keys are read only from the environment and the constructor; waggle
never writes them to disk, and signing happens locally so the key never leaves
your machine. Use the least-privileged key for the task: social actions need
only the posting key, transfers the active key.

A WIF passed as a command-line argument (for example to @code{pubkey}) may be
recorded in your shell history; prefer the environment for secrets. Transfer
memos are plaintext on a public chain. The cryptography is hand-rolled and has
not been independently audited. See @file{SECURITY.md} for the full policy.

